                "HCO₃ ⇌ H⁺ + CO₃²",
                "4.7 x 10⁻¹²",
                "Weak"
              ],
              [
                "H₂O",
                "H₂O ⇌ H⁺ + OH⁻",
                "1.8 x 10⁻¹⁵",
                "Very weak"
              ]
            ],
            "book_errors": [
              "(10⁻²)",
              "(10⁻⁵)",
              "1.3 x 10⁻⁴",
              "6.7 x 10⁻⁵",
              "H₂CO₃ ⇌ H⁺ + HS⁻",
              "NH₄¹",
              "NH₅",
              "4.7 x 10⁻¹²",
              "1.8 x 10⁻¹⁵"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "correction",
            "title": "Book correction",
            "text": "Table 9.3 has these errors. (1) The bracketed values for HCl (10⁻²), HNO₃ (10⁻⁵) and H₂SO₄ (10⁻²) cannot be right: a strong acid has Ka much greater than 1, as the words 'very large' say. (2) HSO₄⁻: Ka is about 1 × 10⁻², not 1.3 × 10⁻⁴. (3) HF: Ka is of the order of 10⁻⁴ (about 6.8 × 10⁻⁴), not 6.7 × 10⁻⁵. (4) H₂CO₃ ionizes to H⁺ + HCO₃⁻, not HS⁻. (5) The ammonium row is NH₄⁺ ⇌ H⁺ + NH₃ (NH₅ does not exist). (6) HCO₃⁻: Ka is 4.7 × 10⁻¹¹, not 4.7 × 10⁻¹². (7) Water: the book itself uses 1.8 × 10⁻¹⁶ in 9.3 (1.0 × 10⁻¹⁴ ÷ 55.5 = 1.8 × 10⁻¹⁶), not 1.8 × 10⁻¹⁵."
          }
        ]
      }
